# Code structure

Apply this discipline in the frontend (`apps/web`, `packages/react`, `packages/shared`).

## Directory map

| Role | Frontend |
| --- | --- |
| Compose: hooks → map data into UI | `apps/web` routes; domain `feature/` |
| Orchestrate: state, actions, derive views | `packages/react/.../hooks/` |
| Work: pure transforms | `.../util/`; isomorphic → `@repo/shared` |
| Present: one visual concern per file | `.../ui/` (compound parents in feature/DS) |
| Frozen literals / lookup tables | `.../constants/` or `.../util/` |
| Small domain shapes + action creators | `.../util/`; isomorphic → `@repo/shared` |
| Tiny SVG components | `.../icons/` |

## Responsibilities

1. **Compose** — call hooks and map the view model into components.
2. **Orchestrate** — hold state, define actions, call `util`, derive view models (`as const`).
3. **Work** — pure functions: input → output, no React.
4. **Present** — props or ambient compound context → markup.

## Data flow

```
user event
  → leaf dispatches action (or calls hook handler)
  → reducer/hook calls util
  → new state
  → hook derives view model in render
  → compose edge maps view model into components
```

**Who iterates:** the compose edge (`feature/` / route) maps collections onto compound children. Compound parents provide layout, context, and default slots — they do not internally `.map` the domain list.

**Who dispatches:** repeating leaves read ambient context and `dispatch(actionCreator(payload))`. The compose edge does not drill `onReorder` / `onRemove` through every row.

## Canonical shape

**Compose** — `feature/` / `apps/web` routes: call hooks, map the view model into nested UI.

```tsx
import { ItemList, Panel } from '@repo/react/design-system';

import { useItems } from '../hooks/use-items';

export function ItemsPanel({ collectionId }: ItemsPanelProps) {
  const { items, dispatch } = useItems({ collectionId });

  return (
    <Panel>
      <ItemList dispatch={dispatch}>
        <ItemList.Toolbar />
        {items.map((item) => (
          <ItemList.Row key={item.id} item={item} />
        ))}
      </ItemList>
    </Panel>
  );
}
```

**Orchestrate** — `hooks/`: discriminated `Action`, creators, reducer that calls `util`, derives the view model in render (`react-feature-hooks.mdc`).

**Work** — `util/`: one concern each — merge, validate, path builders, array updates (`pure-domain.mdc`).

**Present** — `ui/` leaves: read props or ambient data, render one control (`tiny-files.mdc`). Layout uses design-system primitives (`design-system-layout.mdc`).

Named exports; options objects for 2+ params (`function-args.mdc`); domain folders under `packages/react/src/<domain>/` with `feature/` / `ui/` / `util/` / `hooks/` (no dangling files at the domain root).

## Refactor checklist

- [ ] File lives in `feature/` / `ui/` / `hooks/` / `util/` / `data-access/` / `constants/` / `icons/` — not at the domain root
- [ ] Pure logic lives in `util/` / `@repo/shared`
- [ ] Hook wires and derives; util does the work
- [ ] UI leaf is one concern (`tiny-files.mdc`)
- [ ] Variation uses slots / composition (`react-composition.mdc`)
- [ ] Layout uses DS primitives; no public `className` / `style` (`design-system-layout.mdc`)
- [ ] Collections are mapped at the compose edge; leaves dispatch via context
- [ ] Named `handleX` / derived consts in the hook body; `return` only composes them — no `useCallback` / `useMemo` for stability (`react-feature-hooks.mdc`)

## Sibling rules

| Rule | Covers |
| --- | --- |
| `tiny-files.mdc` | Size budgets, filename hierarchy, co-located privates |
| `pure-domain.mdc` | `util` catalog, composing pure helpers |
| `react-feature-hooks.mdc` | Actions, reducers, effects, naming, compiler |
| `react-handlers.mdc` | `onClick={handleClick}` vs inline |
| `react-layers.mdc` | `feature` / `ui` / `hooks` / `util` / `data-access` |
| `react-composition.mdc` | Compounds, slots, context, HTML props |
| `react-hook-injection.mdc` | Inject hooks into reusable compounds via props |
| `react-compound-e2e.mdc` | Full compound assembly from files to compose edge |
| `design-system-layout.mdc` | DS primitives; Mantine only inside DS; `Button` / `Input` / `Pin` |
| `imports-and-files.mdc` | Kebab-case, named exports, shallow imports |
| `types-and-constants.mdc` | Types, constants, `as const` / `satisfies` |
| `function-args.mdc` | Options-object args |
